{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014gMCWVBbT1EosPtJm6FjBx","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Working notes\n2\t\n3\t## Emoji data and search\n4\t\n5\t- `src/data.ts` is the adapter boundary for the Emoji Mart JSON dataset.\n6\t  Keep the public `EmojiEntry` fields compatible with custom emoji data.\n7\t- `src/search.ts` owns the shared ranking order: name prefix, name\n8\t  substring, then keyword prefix.\n9\t- Changes to the data adapter should be checked with `npm run lint`,\n10\t  `npx tsc --noEmit --project tsconfig.json`, and the browser test bundle.\n11\t\n12\t## Picker component conventions\n13\t\n14\t- Picker DOM stays light-DOM; its styles are injected once per document or\n15\t  shadow root through `adoptedStyleSheets`.\n16\t- Picker UI tokens use the `--emoji-picker-*` namespace so host styles can\n17\t  theme the panel without relying on internal class names.\n18\t- Picker category filtering should consume `EmojiEntry.category` or\n19\t  `EmojiEntry.categories`, while text filtering should use `src/search.ts`.\n20\t\n21\t## Component exports\n22\t\n23\t- Public custom elements should register from their component module and keep\n24\t  their DOM in light DOM with styles injected through adopted stylesheets.\n25\t- Adding a public component requires updating the main entrypoint and its\n26\t  explicit package subpath together so ESM and CommonJS builds agree.\n27\t## Picker state and interaction\n28\t\n29\t- Persisted picker preferences should use configurable attributes and guard\n30\t  every `localStorage` read and write with an in-memory fallback.\n31\t- Picker interaction tests should query public roles such as `gridcell`,\n32\t  `radio`, and `status`, rather than component class names or private fields.\n33\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"16829455-2d54-4b61-851e-96b311024956","uuid":"1600efd7-ee77-44ad-8677-c1226aebf6e1","timestamp":"2026-09-23T18:38:05.798Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/nick/code/emoji-input.correctness-audit-fixes-02-shared-placement-helper/AGENTS.md","content":"# Working notes\n\n## Emoji data and search\n\n- `src/data.ts` is the adapter boundary for the Emoji Mart JSON dataset.\n  Keep the public `EmojiEntry` fields compatible with custom emoji data.\n- `src/search.ts` owns the shared ranking order: name prefix, name\n  substring, then keyword prefix.\n- Changes to the data adapter should be checked with `npm run lint`,\n  `npx tsc --noEmit --project tsconfig.json`, and the browser test bundle.\n\n## Picker component conventions\n\n- Picker DOM stays light-DOM; its styles are injected once per document or\n  shadow root through `adoptedStyleSheets`.\n- Picker UI tokens use the `--emoji-picker-*` namespace so host styles can\n  theme the panel without relying on internal class names.\n- Picker category filtering should consume `EmojiEntry.category` or\n  `EmojiEntry.categories`, while text filtering should use `src/search.ts`.\n\n## Component exports\n\n- Public custom elements should register from their component module and keep\n  their DOM in light DOM with styles injected through adopted stylesheets.\n- Adding a public component requires updating the main entrypoint and its\n  explicit package subpath together so ESM and CommonJS builds agree.\n## Picker state and interaction\n\n- Persisted picker preferences should use configurable attributes and guard\n  every `localStorage` read and write with an in-memory fallback.\n- Picker interaction tests should query public roles such as `gridcell`,\n  `radio`, and `status`, rather than component class names or private fields.\n","numLines":33,"startLine":1,"totalLines":33}}}
